Wiring:
- DHT22 module VCC -> ESP32 3V3.
- DHT22 module DATA -> GPIO4.
- DHT22 module GND -> ESP32 GND.
- GPIO23 -> 220 ohm resistor -> LED anode.
- LED cathode -> GND.

Because the DHT22 module already includes its DATA pull-up, do not add another resistor. Powering the module from 3.3 V keeps the DATA high level within the ESP32's 3.3 V logic range.

```cpp
#include <DHT.h>

const int DHT_PIN = 4;
const int LED_PIN = 23;
#define DHT_TYPE DHT22

DHT dht(DHT_PIN, DHT_TYPE);

void setup() {
  pinMode(LED_PIN, OUTPUT);
  digitalWrite(LED_PIN, LOW);
  dht.begin();
}

void loop() {
  float temperatureC = dht.readTemperature();

  if (isnan(temperatureC)) {
    digitalWrite(LED_PIN, LOW);
  } else {
    digitalWrite(LED_PIN, temperatureC >= 30.0 ? HIGH : LOW);
  }

  delay(2000);
}
```

The DHT22 should not be polled rapidly; a 2-second interval is appropriate for this sensor.

